sident GLBs. Existing reconstructed Otis Bardwell, Joseph Dufresne and Martin Flynn remain the study identities; clothing and appearance remain reconstructed. The broader T-1789 ticket stays open.\n\nIndependent source review and 16 actual source-swap preview images show the observed trouser/shoulder/collar/toe defects repaired. Forty inherited negative face projections remain in the defined idle sample (minimum -8.98 mm). Full garment fit across LODs and motions, finer period tailoring and photographic quality remain open.\n\nValidation: full local preflight passed all 1,038 checks (380 deliberate refusal self-tests); exact-commit changelog/ID checks passed, including the authoring-only trailer on the human commit itself. Canonical run [39687040336](https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/actions/runs/39687040336) succeeded at this exact source commit, attempt 1, with both build inputs true. Its mandatory jobs, 48 source/published inspections, 24 sole receipts, six seated runs, three refusals, W01 source/published checks and 24 container validations were independently qualified. All normal PR check runs at this source commit also passed; DEV-base reconciliation remains required before merge. Root viewed the same-run Bardwell web standing-quarter, close-face and seated-quarter images: the coverage/shoe/eye repairs exported, while tight/crude period garments and face/hair/skin quality remain below the photographic target. No scene figure or occupied acceptance is added. No threshold or reader assertion is weakened.\n\nTarget is DEV only. No production promotion.\n\nDependency: this branch includes the reviewed parked parent commit from PR #1174, currently blocked by two confidence-view driver-budget assertions in its desktop part 13 smoke. The PR remains draft. The canonical run is now terminal. After the parent lands, reconcile DEV ancestry without changing reviewed human inputs, regenerate, and re-gate before merge. No duplicate parked acceptance or parent-ticket completion is claimed.\n\nSource checkpoint: `2f75ef23dbb316ebe4cf53e65ce3af8b04f140d3`. Recovery evidence: https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago-tickets/tree/main/evidence/parked-vehicles-2026-10-21 .\n\nCorrected preview finding (2026-10-22): missing seated shoes in the V2 source preview came from stale idle SkinnedMesh bounds. Finite CPU replay and actual corrected V3 captures agree; production HumanActor already disables skinned frustum culling. The corrected V3 inspection passed all 24 framing and shoe-render guards with zero page errors. A separate V6 level-hem source preview also passed 24 images, framing and shoe-render guards; selected standing and seated views show cleaner cuffs. Both browsers closed. V5/V6 remain unapplied and are excluded from this PR's canonical qualification. Complete ankle enclosure, 40 inherited idle negative projections, full LOD/motion fit, fine period tailoring and photographic quality remain open. Original failed previews and their exact inputs are preserved with the corrected evidence. No town figure is enabled.\n","created_at":"2026-10-21T22:29:26Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T01:20:27Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"22f30f3d43e3c1e804f3525766b78cc820e61747","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/pulls/1175/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/pulls/1175/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/issues/1175/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/statuses/2f75ef23dbb316ebe4cf53e65ce3af8b04f140d3","head":{"label":"kevinrhaas:steward/1835-workwear-repair-20261021","ref":"steward/1835-workwear-repair-20261021","sha":"2f75ef23dbb316ebe4cf53e65ce3af8b04f140d3","user":{"login":"kevinrhaas","